findings.body:
Removing `@require_role("admin")` leaves `DELETE /users/<user>` with no authorization check. Any client that can reach this route can delete any user and get `204`, including viewer-scoped cleanup jobs and unauthenticated callers.

That is an access-control bypass on a destructive endpoint. Fix the cleanup-job 403 by giving the job a principal that is allowed to delete (dedicated role, service credential, or separate internal handler), and keep a require-role (or equivalent) guard on this route.

```suggestion
@require_role("admin")
def delete_user(user):
```
